RECORD  alternatives with a producer                                81
RECORD  NOT RUN: [people] tile: photo <lookup> skipped: <why>       the Contacts provider decodes a photo when it is written, so no fixture can store an undecodable one (r3 V6) — JVM: PeopleTileRulesTest (app/src/test/kotlin/app/tileshell/feeds/PeopleTileRulesTest.kt)
RECORD  NOT RUN: [people] link <a>+<b>: refused (not allowed)       Link / Unlink with another profile's contact is refused by the guard (fix-round F23), and no page offers it: a work-profile card has no Link action (E16 asserts its card's actions), so the refusal cannot be reached from the UI — JVM: PeopleWriterTest (app/src/test/kotlin/app/tileshell/people/PeopleWriterTest.kt)
RECORD  NOT RUN: [people] write insert raw=new: failed the phone's default account for new contacts is a cloud account, so it refuses one saved to the phone  said only on a phone whose default account for new contacts is a cloud one (Android 16's rule); the AVD has no such default, and one cannot be set from adb without an account's authenticator on the image — JVM: PeopleWriterTest (app/src/test/kotlin/app/tileshell/people/PeopleWriterTest.kt) — aPhoneWhoseDefaultAccountIsACloudOneRefusesASaveToThePhoneBeforeAnythingIsWritten (asserts the result and that nothing was written; the line's text is not asserted)
RECORD  NOT RUN: [people] write delete raw=<id>: ok (taken back)    the take-back runs only when the phone files a new contact under another account than the one asked for: the AVD's Contacts provider files a new contact (and a new group) in the account it is asked for — E13's create leg, E27's create leg and E15's SIM leg assert exactly that, with no delete after — and nothing sent over adb makes a provider file an insert under another account — JVM: PeopleWriterTest (app/src/test/kotlin/app/tileshell/people/PeopleWriterTest.kt) — aNewContactThePhoneFilesUnderAnotherAccountIsTakenBackAndTheSaveFails (asserts this line's text)
RECORD  NOT RUN: [people] write insert raw=<id>: failed <why>; it was taken back  the same path as the line above: the AVD's Contacts provider files a new contact (and a new group) in the account it is asked for — E13's create leg, E27's create leg and E15's SIM leg assert exactly that, with no delete after — and nothing sent over adb makes a provider file an insert under another account — JVM: PeopleWriterTest (app/src/test/kotlin/app/tileshell/people/PeopleWriterTest.kt) — aNewContactThePhoneFilesUnderAnotherAccountIsTakenBackAndTheSaveFails (asserts this line's text); aNewContactThatCannotBeReadBackIsTakenBack; aNewContactFiledUnderAnotherAccountIsTakenBackEvenWhenPeopleMayWriteThatAccount
RECORD  NOT RUN: [people] write delete raw=<id>: failed (removed <n>)  a take-back whose own delete fails: it needs the path above AND a delete the provider does not carry out — JVM: PeopleWriterTest (app/src/test/kotlin/app/tileshell/people/PeopleWriterTest.kt) — aTakeBackThatFailsSaysTheContactIsStillThere (drives the delete throwing and removing nothing; asserts no line says ok; this line's text is not asserted)
RECORD  NOT RUN: [people] write insert raw=<id>: failed <why>; it could NOT be taken back - still in <type:name>  the same path as the line above — JVM: PeopleWriterTest (app/src/test/kotlin/app/tileshell/people/PeopleWriterTest.kt) — aTakeBackThatFailsSaysTheContactIsStillThere (asserts the line's ending)
RECORD  NOT RUN: [people] write insert raw=<id>: failed <why>; whether it was taken back is not known  a take-back whose delete removes nothing while the row can no longer be read: not makeable on a device — JVM: PeopleWriterTest (app/src/test/kotlin/app/tileshell/people/PeopleWriterTest.kt) — aTakeBackWhoseOutcomeCannotBeReadSaysItIsNotKnown (asserts the result and this line's text; added in commit 100b7d8e)
RECORD  NOT RUN: [people] write insert raw=<id>: failed <why>; no id to take back  an insert that returns an id of 0 or less: no provider on a device answers so — JVM: PeopleWriterTest (app/src/test/kotlin/app/tileshell/people/PeopleWriterTest.kt) — anInsertThatReturnsNoRealIdIsNotFollowedByADelete (asserts no delete is issued and the line's ending; added in commit 100b7d8e); aTakeBackNeedsAnIdAnInsertReallyReturned (the guard's verdict for ids 0 and -1)
RECORD  NOT RUN: [people] group create new: failed the phone's default account for new contacts is a cloud account, so it refuses one saved to the phone  as for a contact: only on a phone whose default account for new contacts is a cloud one — JVM: PeopleWriterTest (app/src/test/kotlin/app/tileshell/people/PeopleWriterTest.kt) — aNewGroupThePhoneFilesUnderAnotherAccountIsTakenBack (its last part asserts the result and that nothing was written; the line's text is not asserted)
RECORD  NOT RUN: [people] write delete group=<id>: ok (taken back)  the take-back of a new group the phone filed under another account: the AVD's Contacts provider files a new contact (and a new group) in the account it is asked for — E13's create leg, E27's create leg and E15's SIM leg assert exactly that, with no delete after — and nothing sent over adb makes a provider file an insert under another account — JVM: PeopleWriterTest (app/src/test/kotlin/app/tileshell/people/PeopleWriterTest.kt) — aNewGroupThePhoneFilesUnderAnotherAccountIsTakenBack (asserts the delete call and that the group is gone; this line's text is not asserted)
RECORD  NOT RUN: [people] group create <id>: failed <why>; it was taken back  the same path as the line above — JVM: PeopleWriterTest (app/src/test/kotlin/app/tileshell/people/PeopleWriterTest.kt) — aNewGroupThePhoneFilesUnderAnotherAccountIsTakenBack (asserts this line's text)
RECORD  NOT RUN: [people] group create <id>: failed <why>; it could NOT be taken back - still in <type:name>  a group's take-back whose delete fails — JVM: PeopleWriterTest (app/src/test/kotlin/app/tileshell/people/PeopleWriterTest.kt) — aNewGroupThePhoneFilesUnderAnotherAccountIsTakenBack (its "removes nothing" part asserts the result's leftBehind; the line's text is not asserted)
RECORD  NOT RUN: [calendar] sync event=<id> -> calendar <id>: refused (not allowed)  no page offers a Sync the guard refuses: the picker lists only the calendars allowed on "Can sync to" (E23), and a synced event whose target left that list opens "Can sync to" instead of writing — driven in E24 leg D (the `no calendar allowed -> can sync to` line, no `-> calendar <id>:` line, the copy's row untouched) — so the refusal cannot be reached from the app — JVM: CalendarWriteLayerTest (app/src/test/kotlin/app/tileshell/calendar/CalendarWriteLayerTest.kt)
RECORD  NOT RUN: [calendar] sync event=<id> -> calendar <id>: failed the copy could not be read  a copy row the provider cannot return while its mapping stands cannot be made from adb: a copy deleted or moved on the other side reads as gone (recreated, E24) or stale (EDGE C04), never unreadable (fix-round F30) — JVM: CalendarWriteLayerTest (app/src/test/kotlin/app/tileshell/calendar/CalendarWriteLayerTest.kt)
